{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 25430751576a9563797f245e45a79abd56d66f8f on planner/selfhost-drain-20261108, one commit on main f1ec237c, with artifact 384c28eb on notes/2026-10-19-self-hosting-on-celld.md, for request 33873e49 under planner promise 47976f0a and review request dfa5dac5. Draft 4 adds a drain rule for a node with no live peer and states the waker's delay. Each new fact matches its source.\n\nChecked against the sources:\n\n- The single-node drain. The SeaweedFS evaluation, section 3, records it: every SIGTERM logged `shutdown_handoff_stalled` after 25 s, no `node-log close: sealed epoch` line was written, and `nodes/mini-1.json` stayed with `\"draining\": true` and no `log` object. The saved celld v0.6.3 guarantees.md, lines 126-128, names the three record states that count the stopped process's node log as recovered: absent, no `log` object, or `\"state\": \"sealed\"`. The new 4.7 rule uses exactly those three. It keeps an open or recovering `log` object as an unknown drain. Its recovery by the same node name during startup matches guarantees.md line 123.\n- The Mac path. docs/self-host.md, \"Run on a Mac\", says that a normal exit leaves celld stopped \"so a preserve shutdown can finish\". That is the other one-node path that the new paragraph names.\n- The waker. The evaluation records 2 ms in a resident cell and 20.2 s through a cold wake. guarantees.md lines 330-332 give the 60-second default and `CELLD_WAKER_TICK_MS`. The new sentence says that a shorter interval lists the bucket more often. That follows from the same lines, which say that each pass lists the bucket.\n- The status line. d6967b7f is the first-parent commit on main of 27 October that contains e44e38f0, which added apps/room/celld. So \"Slice H1 ... landed at d6967b7f\" holds.\n- Consistency. Section 5's `drain.sh` row, H4's added witness, decision 9 and section 12's two finding rows state the same rule. Section 13 cites guarantees.md at the v0.6.3 tag.\n\nChecks: the